#NEXUS

[ yu2018a_fig5: Oviraptorosaur summary tree, 11 tips, fully resolved. Root at the bottom of the vertical trunk; Caud. and Avim. branch off its lower end, Micr. and the Anzu./Anom./Giga. clade at its top, and the oviraptorid branch leaves the trunk part-way up. Several tips (Conc., Wula., Anom.) sit on short vertical stalks directly above their nodes. Tip names are the printed abbreviations, which no matrix lists. Random-sample case (seed 20261106); the only slanted figure with a time axis left in the census. Topology transcribed from the figure and checked node by node at 3x; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=11;
    TAXLABELS
        Caud.
        Avim.
        Micr.
        Anzu.
        Anom.
        Giga.
        Nank.
        Citi.
        Wula.
        Conc.
        Neme.
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE yu2018a_fig5 = [&R] (Caud.,(Avim.,((Micr.,(Anzu.,(Anom.,Giga.))),(Nank.,(Citi.,(Wula.,(Conc.,Neme.)))))));
END;
